  m_Name: Cookie Cutter Shark
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  fishName: Cookie-Cutter Shark
  fishSmallDescription: 'Cookiecutter shark (Isistius brasiliensis) is a deep-sea
    shark that is quite tiny. Despite its small size, it can be a very dangerous
    little guy.   known for taking circular bites out of much larger animals and
    even submarines. '
  infoWhere: These guys stay at a range between 1000 - 3,700m. Usually, they swim
    around in the open water as they look for food.
  fishFullDescription: "Surprised you managed to scan this one without getting bit
    to pieces.\r\n\r\nThe cookiecutter shark is a tiny 40-50cm fish that shouldn\u2019t
    be under estimated. As can be told from their name they are famous for taking
    cookie shaped bites from larger fish.\r\n\r\nDuring day time it stays around
    1000 - 3700 meters but at night it ventures closer to the surface to find food.
    They do this as not venturing up during the daytime increases their chances of
    not getting eaten by a bigger predator. \r\n"
